From 5b70bac1b8616c39cd3756659b499935b9746aeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Bassett <abassett@qnx.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Feb 2026 18:24:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] QNX port

Imported from qnx-ports/nss (NSS_3_131_1_RTM...5b70bac1b861, branch
qnx-NSS_3_131_1_BRANCH); original authorship kept. The branch's other
commit (60747ce8d83d, "update gtest to v1.17.0") only touches the gtests,
which this port does not build, and is left out.

gyp knows no OS "qnx": treat it like FreeBSD (BSD flock, the FREEBSD code
paths), build freebl's AES/GHASH with -mpclmul -maes as on the other ELF
systems, C++17 instead of C++11 (QNX's libc++ needs it), take the byte-order
helpers from <net/netbyte.h> (QNX has no <endian.h>), and rename variables
called "bool", which <stdbool.h> (pulled in by QNX's headers) defines as a macro.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific (carried in the qnx-ports fork)
---
diff --git a/nss/cmd/multinit/multinit.c b/nss/cmd/multinit/multinit.c
index c6c40e94d..85efc771b 100644
--- a/nss/cmd/multinit/multinit.c
+++ b/nss/cmd/multinit/multinit.c
@@ -282,13 +282,13 @@ appendString(char *string)
  * append a bool, T= true, F=false
  */
 static void
-appendBool(PRBool bool)
+appendBool(PRBool m_bool)
 {
     if (!buffer.data) {
         return;
     }
 
-    if (bool) {
+    if (m_bool) {
         appendLabel('t');
     } else {
         appendLabel('f');
@@ -385,9 +385,9 @@ usage_long(const char *prog)
 }
 
 static const char *
-bool2String(PRBool bool)
+bool2String(PRBool m_bool)
 {
-    return bool ? "true" : "false";
+    return m_bool ? "true" : "false";
 }
 
 /*
